# mksquashfs -ef excludes (live-build passes -wildcards, so entries must be
# paths RELATIVE to the squashfs root: a leading / is a FATAL ERROR:
#   "FATAL ERROR: /, ./ and ../ prefixed excludes not supported with
#    -wildcards or -regex options"
# That cost a full build (#36) before test/stages/stage-a.sh learned to check
# it. Do not add a leading slash here.
#
# Everything a *build* needs but a *booted image* must not carry.
#
# var/cache/klh-pool is filled by zzz-klh-deb-pool.hook.chroot (~900MB of the
# build's own .deb files) so the host can harvest them into the
# content-addressed pool after the build. Shipping it would nearly double the
# ISO; it exists only between the chroot hook and build.sh's harvest step.
var/cache/klh-pool
